cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Graph2Text AML: graph-conditioned generation of Suspicious Activity Report narratives"
abstract: >-
  Graph2Text AML generates human-readable Suspicious Activity Report (SAR) narratives
  from financial transaction subgraphs flagged as suspicious, shifting anti-money-
  laundering model output from opaque classification to investigator-usable explanation.
  The system couples a graph attention encoder to a QLoRA-finetuned large language model
  through a learned fusion layer, and is trained on a three-tier corpus constructed for
  this work because no corpus of (graph, SAR narrative) pairs exists publicly.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE_ME/graph2text-aml"
